WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:11.000
This is the beginning of Volume 2, and it begins with February 28, 1899.

2
00:00:11.000 --> 00:00:26.000
Louisa says, "I confess the truth. I feel great repugnance. The effort I have to make in order to conquer myself is so great that the Lord alone can know the torture of my soul."

3
00:00:26.000 --> 00:00:34.000
O Holy Obedience, what a powerful bond you are, you alone could win over me,

4
00:00:34.000 --> 00:00:44.000
and surpassing all my repugnance, almost impassable mountains, you bind me to the will of God and to the Confessor.

5
00:00:44.000 --> 00:00:52.000
But please, O Holy Spouse, as great as my sacrifices, so much help do I need.

6
00:00:52.000 --> 00:01:04.000
I want nothing but that you hold me in your arms and sustain me. That is, Philippians 4, 13, I can do all things in Christ who gives me the strength.

7
00:01:04.000 --> 00:01:09.000
And John 15, 5, without him, I can do nothing.

8
00:01:09.000 --> 00:01:21.000
In this way, assisted by you, I will be able to say only the truth that's John 14, 6, only for your glory and for my confusion.

9
00:01:21.000 --> 00:01:28.000
This morning, since the Confessor celebrated Mass, I also received communion.

10
00:01:28.000 --> 00:01:38.000
My mind was in a sea of confusion because of disobedience and that the Confessor gave me, to write everything that passes in my interior.

11
00:01:38.000 --> 00:01:46.000
As I received Jesus, I began to tell him of my pains, especially of my insufficiency and many other things.

12
00:01:46.000 --> 00:01:52.000
But Jesus did not seem to care about this thing of mine and did not answer to anything.

13
00:01:52.000 --> 00:02:04.000
A light came to my mind. Now, this is enlightenment or infused knowledge, but God is light, 1 John 1, 5.

14
00:02:04.000 --> 00:02:13.000
And I said, "Who knows whether I am myself and the cause for which Jesus is not showing himself as usual."

15
00:02:13.000 --> 00:02:21.000
So with all my heart, I said to him, "Oh, please, my good and my all, don't show yourself so indifferent to me.

16
00:02:21.000 --> 00:02:26.000
You make my heart split with pain."

17
00:02:26.000 --> 00:02:34.000
If it is because of the writing, let it be, let it be, even if it costs me the sacrifice of my life, I promise I will do it.

18
00:02:34.000 --> 00:02:40.000
Then Jesus changed appearance and all benign, he said to me, "What do you fear?"

19
00:02:40.000 --> 00:02:46.000
Have I not assisted you at other times? My light will surround you everywhere.

20
00:02:46.000 --> 00:02:58.000
Now, that's Psalm 21, sorry, Psalm 27 verse 1, "Send forth your light and your truth, let these be my guide."

21
00:02:58.000 --> 00:03:06.000
In the higher volumes, Jesus will have Louisa say that Jesus himself dictated everything to her.

22
00:03:06.000 --> 00:03:13.000
My light will surround you everywhere, and so you will be able to do it.

23
00:03:13.000 --> 00:03:20.000
So the next topic has a heading called "Purity of Intention."

24
00:03:20.000 --> 00:03:27.000
While he was saying this, I don't know how I saw the Confessor near Jesus, and the Lord said to him,

25
00:03:27.000 --> 00:03:35.000
"See, everything you do passes. Everything you do passes into heaven."

26
00:03:35.000 --> 00:03:45.000
Therefore, see with what purity you must operate, thinking that all of your steps, words, and works come before my presence.

27
00:03:45.000 --> 00:03:52.000
And if they are pure, that is, if they are done for me, I will take delight in them,

28
00:03:52.000 --> 00:04:00.000
and I will feel them around me like many messengers that remind me continuously of you.

29
00:04:00.000 --> 00:04:08.000
Okay, I want to give you Hebrews 12, 14, nothing unholy or unworthy can enter the presence of God.

30
00:04:08.000 --> 00:04:16.000
I want to give you Matthew 5, 8, only the pure in heart, see God.

31
00:04:16.000 --> 00:04:24.000
And I want to give you John 14, 31, where Jesus said, "I want the world to know that I love the Father,

32
00:04:24.000 --> 00:04:28.000
and therefore I will do exactly as my Father tells me."

33
00:04:28.000 --> 00:04:34.000
But if they are not, if they are done, Jesus said, for low and earthly reasons.

34
00:04:34.000 --> 00:04:38.000
In other words, the purity of intention isn't there.

35
00:04:38.000 --> 00:04:41.000
I feel bothered by them.

36
00:04:41.000 --> 00:04:46.000
And as he was saying this, he seemed to grab his hands, this is the priest's hands,

37
00:04:46.000 --> 00:04:53.000
and raising them up to heaven, he said, "Your eyes always on high, you are of heaven, work for heaven."

38
00:04:53.000 --> 00:04:57.000
So here's the motto that Jesus gave the priest, and he's giving to us,

39
00:04:57.000 --> 00:05:02.000
that we have to keep our eyes on God, not on the things of the earth,

40
00:05:02.000 --> 00:05:08.000
because we are of heaven, and we must work for heaven.

41
00:05:08.000 --> 00:05:13.000
So Louisa said, "As I was seeing the Confessor and Jesus saying this to him,

42
00:05:13.000 --> 00:05:18.000
in my mind it seemed to me as if one operated in that way,

43
00:05:18.000 --> 00:05:22.000
it would happen us to a person who had to leave one house and move to another."

44
00:05:22.000 --> 00:05:24.000
What does he do?

45
00:05:24.000 --> 00:05:28.000
First he sends all of his things and everything he possesses,

46
00:05:28.000 --> 00:05:30.000
and then he goes himself.

47
00:05:30.000 --> 00:05:37.000
In the same way, if we first send our works to take a place in heaven for us,

48
00:05:37.000 --> 00:05:42.000
and then when our time comes, we go ourselves.

49
00:05:42.000 --> 00:05:46.000
Or what a beautiful courtage they will make for us.

50
00:05:46.000 --> 00:05:49.000
In other words, the only things we can take to heaven with us

51
00:05:49.000 --> 00:05:54.000
are things that are of God, and about God, and for him.

52
00:05:54.000 --> 00:05:58.000
We can take nothing of the earth, we can take nothing of selfishness,

53
00:05:58.000 --> 00:06:04.000
we can take nothing of the ego, we can take nothing of sin with us.

54
00:06:04.000 --> 00:06:10.000
All of that is excess baggage and doesn't belong to the kingdom of God.

55
00:06:10.000 --> 00:06:15.000
So the topic for the next section is faith.

56
00:06:15.000 --> 00:06:19.000
Now, while seeing the Confessor, I remembered that he had told me

57
00:06:19.000 --> 00:06:24.000
that I was to write about faith, in the way in which the Lord had spoken to me

58
00:06:24.000 --> 00:06:26.000
about this virtue.

59
00:06:26.000 --> 00:06:31.000
While I was thinking of this, in one instant the Lord drew me so close to himself

60
00:06:31.000 --> 00:06:37.000
that I felt I was outside of myself, that is in and out of the body experience,

61
00:06:37.000 --> 00:06:40.000
in the vault of the heavens together with Jesus.

62
00:06:40.000 --> 00:06:48.000
And he told me these exact words, "Faith is God."

63
00:06:48.000 --> 00:06:50.000
That is very, very interesting.

64
00:06:50.000 --> 00:06:56.000
You're going to hear him saying, "I am faith, I am hope, I am love, I am grace."

65
00:06:56.000 --> 00:06:59.000
You're going to hear him saying that.

66
00:06:59.000 --> 00:07:07.000
So that when we are asking God for faith, we're asking him to give us his eyes

67
00:07:07.000 --> 00:07:10.000
to see the things of heaven.

68
00:07:10.000 --> 00:07:13.000
"Faith is God," he said.

69
00:07:13.000 --> 00:07:20.000
And these two words contained an immense light such that it is impossible to explain them.

70
00:07:20.000 --> 00:07:22.000
But I'll do what I can.

71
00:07:22.000 --> 00:07:28.000
In the word faith, I understood that faith is God himself.

72
00:07:28.000 --> 00:07:33.000
Just as material food gives life to the body so that it may not die,

73
00:07:33.000 --> 00:07:36.000
faith gives life to the soul.

74
00:07:36.000 --> 00:07:39.000
Without faith, the soul is dead.

75
00:07:39.000 --> 00:07:45.000
Faith vivifies, faith sanctifies, faith spiritualizes man.

76
00:07:45.000 --> 00:07:50.000
And faith makes him keep his eyes fixed on the supreme being in such a way

77
00:07:50.000 --> 00:07:54.000
that he learns nothing of the things of earth.

78
00:07:54.000 --> 00:07:56.000
That's called down here.

79
00:07:56.000 --> 00:08:00.000
And if he learns them, he learns them in God.

80
00:08:00.000 --> 00:08:07.000
Or the happiness of the soul who lives of faith and by faith.

81
00:08:07.000 --> 00:08:13.000
Now, the scripture says that the just man lives by faith.

82
00:08:13.000 --> 00:08:17.000
Her flight is always towards heaven.

83
00:08:17.000 --> 00:08:24.000
In everything that happens to her, she always looks at herself in God.

84
00:08:24.000 --> 00:08:31.000
And so, just as in tribulation, faith raises her to God and she does not afflict herself.

85
00:08:31.000 --> 00:08:33.000
Not even with the lament.

86
00:08:33.000 --> 00:08:41.000
Knowing that she's not to form her contentment down here on earth, but in heaven.

87
00:08:41.000 --> 00:08:46.000
In the same way, if joy reaches and pleasures surround her,

88
00:08:46.000 --> 00:08:50.000
faith raises her to God.

89
00:08:50.000 --> 00:08:56.000
And she says to herself, "Oh, how much more content and rich I will be in heaven."

90
00:08:56.000 --> 00:09:00.000
Now, first of all, let me give you Hebrews chapter 11,

91
00:09:00.000 --> 00:09:07.000
where the author gives us a whole list of all the heroes of faith throughout the scriptures.

92
00:09:07.000 --> 00:09:15.000
Secondly, there have been many rich people who are actually canonized saints,

93
00:09:15.000 --> 00:09:20.000
kings and queens and princes and princesses and so on.

94
00:09:20.000 --> 00:09:26.000
So, that money itself is not the problem.

95
00:09:26.000 --> 00:09:30.000
Satan uses money, sex and power to bring us down.

96
00:09:30.000 --> 00:09:33.000
Not because there's anything wrong with money per se.

97
00:09:33.000 --> 00:09:38.000
If it's used properly, there's nothing wrong with sex per se if it's used properly.

98
00:09:38.000 --> 00:09:43.000
And there's nothing wrong with power per se if it's used properly.

99
00:09:43.000 --> 00:09:49.000
But unfortunately, these three great things can be used very much by Satan

100
00:09:49.000 --> 00:09:54.000
to bring us down to evil, so we have to really take care of them.

101
00:09:54.000 --> 00:10:01.000
So, the rich person feels bothered about these earthly things.

102
00:10:01.000 --> 00:10:04.000
She despises them and tramples them under foot.

103
00:10:04.000 --> 00:10:09.000
Now, so many rich people all down the centuries because of the teaching,

104
00:10:09.000 --> 00:10:15.000
especially in Luke's Gospel, about the blessing of being poor

105
00:10:15.000 --> 00:10:21.000
and the danger of being rich, which is all over Luke's Gospel.

106
00:10:21.000 --> 00:10:24.000
Many of them have renounced their riches and their privileges

107
00:10:24.000 --> 00:10:31.000
and have entered monasteries and become saints, or they've gone out into the desert.

108
00:10:31.000 --> 00:10:35.000
So, it seems to me that to a soul who lives by faith,

109
00:10:35.000 --> 00:10:39.000
it happens as to a person who possessed millions upon millions of coins

110
00:10:39.000 --> 00:10:44.000
and even entire kingdoms, and someone else wanted to offer him a cent,

111
00:10:44.000 --> 00:10:47.000
what would he say? How would he disdain it?

112
00:10:47.000 --> 00:10:51.000
Would he not disdain it? Would he not throw it in his face?

113
00:10:51.000 --> 00:10:59.000
I add, and what if that cent were all muddy, just as earthly things are?

114
00:10:59.000 --> 00:11:03.000
Even more, what if that cent were only lent to him?

115
00:11:03.000 --> 00:11:09.000
I mean, St. Paul says, "What have you... that you have not received?"

116
00:11:09.000 --> 00:11:14.000
This person would say, "I enjoy and possess immense riches,

117
00:11:14.000 --> 00:11:21.000
and you dared to offer me this miserable cent, so muddy, and only for a short time."

118
00:11:21.000 --> 00:11:26.000
I believe he would quickly remove his gaze from it and he wouldn't accept the gift.

119
00:11:26.000 --> 00:11:31.000
That's what the soul does who lives by faith with regard to earthly things,

120
00:11:31.000 --> 00:11:35.000
so that even though you have to use earthly things and they're useful to you

121
00:11:35.000 --> 00:11:41.000
while you're on your earthly pilgrimage, you don't put your attention there,

122
00:11:41.000 --> 00:11:46.000
you don't put all the importance there.

123
00:11:46.000 --> 00:11:51.000
You put your attention on heaven, which is your destiny, your goal,

124
00:11:51.000 --> 00:11:59.000
and you give your attention to the things of heaven which are going to last forever.

125
00:11:59.000 --> 00:12:03.000
Now, let us go back again to the idea of food.

126
00:12:03.000 --> 00:12:10.000
By taking food, the body is not only sustained but shares in the substance of that food,

127
00:12:10.000 --> 00:12:14.000
which transforms into the body itself.

128
00:12:14.000 --> 00:12:17.000
The same with the soul who lives by faith.

129
00:12:17.000 --> 00:12:23.000
Since faith is God himself, the soul comes to live by God himself,

130
00:12:23.000 --> 00:12:29.000
and by nourishing herself with God, she comes to share in the very substance of God.

131
00:12:29.000 --> 00:12:36.000
And by sharing in him, she comes to resemble him and to be transformed with God himself.

132
00:12:36.000 --> 00:12:41.000
Now, I want to give you Ephesians 3, 16 to 21, where we're built on love

133
00:12:41.000 --> 00:12:44.000
and we grow on love and reach the fullness of Christ,

134
00:12:44.000 --> 00:12:49.000
because faith and love work together, they're inseparable.

135
00:12:49.000 --> 00:12:53.000
So, we're transformed with God himself.

136
00:12:53.000 --> 00:12:58.000
Therefore, it happens to the soul who lives by faith that just as God is holy,

137
00:12:58.000 --> 00:13:01.000
the soul is holy and powerful in God.

138
00:13:01.000 --> 00:13:08.000
Now, that's Leviticus 19, 2, "You shall be holy, for I am holy," says the Lord.

139
00:13:08.000 --> 00:13:15.000
I want to give you two Corinthians 3, 18 as well that we're transformed into the image that we reflect.

140
00:13:15.000 --> 00:13:21.000
And I want to give you, well, we see that in a moment.

141
00:13:21.000 --> 00:13:28.000
So, just as God is holy, the soul is holy, and if God is powerful, then the soul is powerful.

142
00:13:28.000 --> 00:13:33.000
If God is wise and strong and just, then the soul is transformed into that as well.

143
00:13:33.000 --> 00:13:36.000
And so, with all the other attributes of God.

144
00:13:36.000 --> 00:13:39.000
In some, the soul becomes a little God.

145
00:13:39.000 --> 00:13:45.000
That's Psalm 8, "Lord, what is man that you would even care for him? He's nothing."

146
00:13:45.000 --> 00:13:49.000
And you made the whole universe with just your powerful word.

147
00:13:49.000 --> 00:13:52.000
And yet you made us a little less than a God.

148
00:13:52.000 --> 00:14:01.000
You also have Psalm 86 verse 4, I think it is.

149
00:14:01.000 --> 00:14:06.000
I said, "You are God's, all of you sons of the most high."

150
00:14:06.000 --> 00:14:12.000
So, Louisa said, "O blessedness of this soul on earth, and you become more blessed in heaven,

151
00:14:12.000 --> 00:14:19.000
because you will be able to receive the fullness in heaven that you were not able to receive on the earth."

152
00:14:19.000 --> 00:14:20.000
Okay.

153
00:14:20.000 --> 00:14:26.000
So, Louisa continues, "I also understood that the words that the Lord says to his beloved souls,

154
00:14:26.000 --> 00:14:29.000
I will espouse you in faith."

155
00:14:29.000 --> 00:14:36.000
Now, that is Hosea chapter 2 from verse 14. There's a big long passage there in Hosea.

156
00:14:36.000 --> 00:14:39.000
"I will espouse you in the faith."

157
00:14:39.000 --> 00:14:45.000
It means nothing less than the Lord in this mystical marriage comes to endow souls with his own virtues.

158
00:14:45.000 --> 00:14:50.000
He clothes us with his own virtues because we've nothing of ourselves.

159
00:14:50.000 --> 00:14:55.000
It seems to me that it happens as to two spouses.

160
00:14:55.000 --> 00:15:02.000
As they join their properties together, the belongings of one can no longer be distinguished from those of the other,

161
00:15:02.000 --> 00:15:05.000
but both of them become their owners.

162
00:15:05.000 --> 00:15:10.000
However, as in our case, the soul is poor, she's nothing of her own.

163
00:15:10.000 --> 00:15:17.000
All the good comes from the Lord, and he lets her share his possessions.

164
00:15:17.000 --> 00:15:28.000
You will see this in the book of Ezekiel as well. Not sure either the chapter or the verse where the Lord says

165
00:15:28.000 --> 00:15:35.000
that he found the people of Israel like a young girl all by herself out in a field and she had absolutely nothing.

166
00:15:35.000 --> 00:15:37.000
She had no clothes, no nothing.

167
00:15:37.000 --> 00:15:46.000
And that he found her and he cleaned her up and he dressed her up and he made her a princess and he married her and so on.

168
00:15:46.000 --> 00:15:51.000
The marriage, of course, is the covenant that God made with Israel.

169
00:15:51.000 --> 00:16:00.000
So then Louisa continues, "The life of the soul is God. Faith is God.

170
00:16:00.000 --> 00:16:09.000
And the soul, by possessing faith, comes to graft all the other virtues into herself in such a way that faith is like a king in her heart.

171
00:16:09.000 --> 00:16:15.000
And the other virtues remain around this king as the subjects that serve faith.

172
00:16:15.000 --> 00:16:20.000
So without faith, virtues themselves are things that have no life."

173
00:16:20.000 --> 00:16:28.000
So without him, we're nothing. That's John 15, 5. There's no possibility.

174
00:16:28.000 --> 00:16:33.000
He is our everything. We are nothing.

175
00:16:33.000 --> 00:16:40.000
Louisa continues, "It seems to me that God communicates faith to man in two ways.

176
00:16:40.000 --> 00:16:46.000
The first way is in holy baptism. It's given to us as a gift."

177
00:16:46.000 --> 00:16:57.000
That's why all children should be baptized so that this gift is given to them and original sin is taken away and they are given entry into the kingdom of God.

178
00:16:57.000 --> 00:17:07.000
The second is when our blessed God, by unleashing a particle of his own substance into the soul, you see God can only give himself.

179
00:17:07.000 --> 00:17:13.000
There isn't anything outside of him except the things that he made.

180
00:17:13.000 --> 00:17:20.000
And so if we want the fullness, we've got to go into God and let him give us a particle of his own substance.

181
00:17:20.000 --> 00:17:29.000
So he unleashes a particle of his own substance into the soul and communicates to her the power of making miracles.

182
00:17:29.000 --> 00:17:44.000
Now, my book says the virtue, but very often that expression actually means power and it is confusing to just read as virtue.

183
00:17:44.000 --> 00:17:47.000
Because we have a different meaning for the word virtue.

184
00:17:47.000 --> 00:17:55.000
So he communicates to her the power of making miracles like raising the dead, healing the sick, stopping the sun and the light.

185
00:17:55.000 --> 00:18:04.000
Now, the Bible old and New Testament is full of stories of people who have worked these miracles.

186
00:18:04.000 --> 00:18:10.000
So I won't give you all those references, it's the whole Bible.

187
00:18:10.000 --> 00:18:19.000
But if you read Hebrews chapter 11, you'll get a list of many of the miracles that these people actually worked.

188
00:18:19.000 --> 00:18:27.000
Or if only the world had faith, it would change into a terrestrial paradise.

189
00:18:27.000 --> 00:18:32.000
Now, this world is paradise when we are in communion with God.

190
00:18:32.000 --> 00:18:35.000
It is hell when we're outside of communion with God.

191
00:18:35.000 --> 00:18:36.000
It's about that simple.

192
00:18:36.000 --> 00:18:42.000
So paradise is not the physical surroundings that we are in.

193
00:18:42.000 --> 00:18:46.000
You could be living in a palace and living in hell.

194
00:18:46.000 --> 00:18:51.000
You could be living in a hovel and be living in paradise.

195
00:18:51.000 --> 00:18:54.000
It all depends on your relationship with God.

196
00:18:54.000 --> 00:18:58.000
And after him, your relationship with others.

197
00:19:01.000 --> 00:19:10.000
Louisa continues, "Oh, how high and sublime is the flight of the soul who exercises herself in faith?"

198
00:19:10.000 --> 00:19:16.000
It seems to me that by exercising herself in faith, the soul acts like those timid little birds,

199
00:19:16.000 --> 00:19:25.000
which for fear of being caught by hunters or of some other snare, establish their dwelling on the top of trees or in high places.

200
00:19:25.000 --> 00:19:33.000
Then when they are forced to take food, they descend, take the food, and immediately fly back into their high dwelling.

201
00:19:33.000 --> 00:19:38.000
Some of them, more cautious, take the food and don't even eat it on the ground.

202
00:19:38.000 --> 00:19:42.000
But in order to be safer, they carry it up to the top of trees where they swallow it.

203
00:19:42.000 --> 00:19:48.000
Now, there's a lovely passage in Isaiah 57, verse 15, where the Lord says,

204
00:19:48.000 --> 00:19:52.000
"That I live in a high and holy place."

205
00:19:52.000 --> 00:19:57.000
And anyone who wants to come into a deep relationship with God,

206
00:19:57.000 --> 00:20:04.000
he wants to bring each one of us separately as if nobody else existed.

207
00:20:04.000 --> 00:20:09.000
He wants to bring each one of us into a high and holy place with him

208
00:20:09.000 --> 00:20:19.000
so that he can work all his tragedies in us and then when he has accomplished it in us, he will do it through us to the world.

209
00:20:19.000 --> 00:20:32.000
So, Louisa continues, in the same way, the soul who lives by faith is so timid with earthly things, timid meanings, careful, you know, you know the dangers.

210
00:20:32.000 --> 00:20:38.000
